<title>UK: Whessoe board to discuss new bid.</title>
<headline>Whessoe board to discuss new bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British instruments and controls maker Whessoe Plc said on Wednesday its board acknowleged the launch of a new takeover bid for its entire share capital by a Norwegian and Swiss partnership and would be meeting soon.</p>
<p>The board two weeks ago agreed to an offer of 155p per share by British controls giant Siebe Plc, but Norway's Seatex Garex ASA and privately-owned Swiss Endress+Hauser have now tabled a joint cash offer at 175p and bought a 10.6 percent stake in Whessoe on the market.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, Whessoe said its board would be meeting &quot;as soon as practicable to consider this offer and will be communicating with its shareholders promptly thereafter.&quot;</p>
<p>Siebe has yet to respond to the European firm's move.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
